{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.ComplexRogersDilog","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.ComplexRogersDilog","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.ComplexDilogarithmDeriv","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.ComplexDilogarithmInversion"],"declarations":34,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.im_div_ofReal_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.im_div_ofReal_neg","kind":"theorem","line":469,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexRogersDilog.lean#L469-L476","doc":"`Im(p/q) < 0` for a positive real `p` and a `q` above the axis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.im_div_ofReal_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.im_div_ofReal_pos","kind":"theorem","line":461,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexRogersDilog.lean#L461-L467","doc":"`Im(p/q) > 0` for a positive real `p` and a `q` below the axis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.branch_im","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.branch_im","kind":"theorem","line":455,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexRogersDilog.lean#L455-L459","doc":"The imaginary part of the branch expression is `2·arg y − 3·arg(1−y)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.branch_eq_of_window","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.branch_eq_of_window","kind":"theorem","line":436,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexRogersDilog.lean#L436-L453","doc":"**The saddle branch equation, with its integer pinned by a window.**\n\n    2·log y − 3·log(1−y) = ε·2πi\n\nfrom `y² = (1−y)³` alone, plus a `2π`-wide window on the imaginary part. For the\n5₂ cubic `y² = (1−y)³` **is** the cubic — `(1−y)³ − y² = −(y³−2y²+3y−1)`\nidentically — so this is the branch equation with nothing assumed about branches. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.exp_branch_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.exp_branch_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":422,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexRogersDilog.lean#L422-L434","doc":"`y² = (1−y)³` gives `exp(2·log y − 3·log(1−y)) = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.eq_intMul_two_pi_I_of_exp_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.eq_intMul_two_pi_I_of_exp_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":399,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexRogersDilog.lean#L399-L420","doc":"**A window pins the branch integer.** `exp u = 1` and\n`Im u ∈ (2π(n−1), 2π(n+1))` force `u = n·2πi` — the window has width `4π` and\nstill contains only one multiple of `2π`, which is what makes the crude bounds\nthe saddle supplies sufficient. `Re u = 0` comes free; it is not a hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.cRogersL_add_inv_of_im_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.cRogersL_add_inv_of_im_neg","kind":"theorem","line":376,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexRogersDilog.lean#L376-L391","doc":"**Rogers inversion below the real axis.** The mirror of\n`cRogersL_add_inv_of_im_pos`:\n\n    L(z) + L(1/z) = π²/3 − (iπ/2)·log z          for `Im z < 0`\n\nSame cancellation, opposite sign — the two together are the inversion half of the\nanharmonic toolkit. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.cRogersL_add_inv_of_im_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.cRogersL_add_inv_of_im_pos","kind":"theorem","line":358,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexRogersDilog.lean#L358-L374","doc":"**Rogers inversion, with the `log(−z)` eliminated.**\n\n    L(z) + L(1/z) = π²/3 + (iπ/2)·log z          for `Im z > 0`\n\nThe `log²` terms cancel *completely* against the ones in `cRogersL_add_inv`, so\nan inversion pair above the real axis is `π²` plus `π` times a single logarithm —\nno quadratic term at all. This is the form Route 58's link G3 uses, and it is why\nthat link's value has no `log²` in it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.mem_invDomain_of_im_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.mem_invDomain_of_im_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":354,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexRogersDilog.lean#L354-L356","doc":"A point off the real axis is in `invDomain`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.arg_le_pi_div_two_of_re_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.arg_le_pi_div_two_of_re_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":350,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexRogersDilog.lean#L350-L352","doc":"`arg z ≤ π/2` from `0 ≤ Re z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.arg_nonneg_of_im_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.arg_nonneg_of_im_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":345,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexRogersDilog.lean#L345-L348","doc":"`0 ≤ arg z` from `0 ≤ Im z`. Named for readability at the use sites, where\nthe whole point is that the bound needed is a crude sign condition. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.clog_neg_of_im_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.clog_neg_of_im_neg","kind":"theorem","line":338,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexRogersDilog.lean#L338-L343","doc":"`log(−z) = log z + iπ` below the real axis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.clog_neg_of_im_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.clog_neg_of_im_pos","kind":"theorem","line":331,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexRogersDilog.lean#L331-L336","doc":"`log(−z) = log z − iπ` above the real axis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.arg_ne_pi_of_im_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.arg_ne_pi_of_im_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":326,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexRogersDilog.lean#L326-L329","doc":"`arg z ≠ π` as soon as `z` is off the real axis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.clog_cube_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.clog_cube_mul","kind":"theorem","line":284,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexRogersDilog.lean#L284-L317","doc":"**The saddle's log identity, from the window.** If `a³·b = −t` with `t > 0`\nand the two arguments sit in `[0, π/2]` and `[0, π]`, then\n\n    3·log a + log b = log t + iπ\n\nwith no branch correction: the sum of arguments lands in `[0, 5π/2] ⊂ (−π, 3π)`,\nand `π` is the only value there congruent to `π` mod `2π`. The window is not\ntight, which is the point — the bounds needed are crude sign conditions.\n\nApplied to `a₃³·y₁ = −y₃` (`FiveTwoComplexPentagon.saddle_arg_cube'`) this is\nthe angle identity Route 58's link G3 rests on. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.im_eq_pi_of_exp_eq_neg_ofReal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.im_eq_pi_of_exp_eq_neg_ofReal","kind":"theorem","line":257,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexRogersDilog.lean#L257-L282","doc":"**The window lemma.** `exp u` a *negative real* forces `Im u ≡ π (mod 2π)`;\na window of width less than `2π` containing `π` then pins it. `(0, 3π)` is the\nwindow the saddle supplies, and it is far from tight. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.clog_eq_of_exp_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.clog_eq_of_exp_eq","kind":"theorem","line":252,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexRogersDilog.lean#L252-L255","doc":"If `exp u = c` and `Im u` lies in `(−π, π]`, then `u` **is** `log c`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.cRogersL_add_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.cRogersL_add_inv","kind":"theorem","line":222,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexRogersDilog.lean#L222-L239","doc":"**Rogers inversion on `ℂ ∖ [0,∞)`.**\n\n    L(z) + L(1/z) = −π²/6 − ½·log(−z)² + ½·log z·log(−z)\n\n`z ∈ invDomain` is what both `cLiTwoExt` terms and `log(−z)` need; `arg z ≠ π`\nis what `log(1/z) = −log z` needs, and it excludes exactly the negative reals,\nwhere `invDomain` alone would not suffice. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.clog_pentagon_expansions","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.clog_pentagon_expansions","kind":"theorem","line":198,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexRogersDilog.lean#L198-L209","doc":"**The three log expansions hold on the positive real square.**\n\nStated for the two that carry the pentagon's `a₃` term; `a₅`'s companions follow\nby the `x ↔ y` symmetry, which is the reflection of §7g's `Z/2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.pentagon_args_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.pentagon_args_pos","kind":"theorem","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexRogersDilog.lean#L183-L196","doc":"**On `0 < x, y < 1` every pentagon argument is a positive real.**\n\nThe five are `x`, `y`, `(1−x)/(1−xy)`, `1−xy`, `(1−y)/(1−xy)`, and the two\n`1 − aᵢ` that the Rogers derivative also needs are `x(1−y)/(1−xy)` and\n`y(1−x)/(1−xy)`. Positivity of all of them is what makes the log expansions\nunconditional there. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.clog_div_of_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.clog_div_of_pos","kind":"theorem","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexRogersDilog.lean#L175-L181","doc":"`log(a/b) = log a − log b` for positive reals, as complex logarithms. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.clog_mul_of_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.clog_mul_of_pos","kind":"theorem","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexRogersDilog.lean#L167-L173","doc":"`log(ab) = log a + log b` for positive reals, as complex logarithms. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.clog_of_eq_ofReal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.clog_of_eq_ofReal","kind":"theorem","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexRogersDilog.lean#L159-L165","doc":"**The one move every branch condition on the real square makes**: a complex\nexpression that happens to equal a *positive real* has complex logarithm the cast\nof the real logarithm. Everything else is then `Real.log_mul` / `Real.log_div`,\nwith no branch left to choose. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.hasDerivAt_cRogersL_comp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.hasDerivAt_cRogersL_comp","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexRogersDilog.lean#L129-L137","doc":"**The chain rule for `cRogersL`.** This is what assembling the pentagon\nneeds: each of its five arguments is a rational function of the differentiation\nvariable, and the composite's derivative is `L′` at the argument times the\nargument's own derivative. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.hasDerivAt_cRogersL_of_mem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.hasDerivAt_cRogersL_of_mem","kind":"theorem","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexRogersDilog.lean#L121-L127","doc":"`hasDerivAt_cRogersL`, with the four hypotheses collapsed to membership of\n`rogersDomain`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.ofReal_mem_rogersDomain","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.ofReal_mem_rogersDomain","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexRogersDilog.lean#L115-L119","doc":"A real point of `(0,1)` is in the domain — the base region the pentagon is\ncontinued from. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.one_sub_ne_zero_of_mem_rogersDomain","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.one_sub_ne_zero_of_mem_rogersDomain","kind":"theorem","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexRogersDilog.lean#L111-L113","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.ne_zero_of_mem_rogersDomain","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.ne_zero_of_mem_rogersDomain","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexRogersDilog.lean#L108-L109","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.isOpen_rogersDomain","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.isOpen_rogersDomain","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexRogersDilog.lean#L105-L106","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.rogersDomain","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.rogersDomain","kind":"def","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexRogersDilog.lean#L100-L103","doc":"**The domain of `cRogersL`**: `ℂ` with both real cuts `(−∞,0]` and `[1,∞)`\nremoved. `slitPlane` handles `log z`, `notCut` handles both `cLiTwoExt` and\n`log (1−z)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.one_sub_mem_slitPlane_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.one_sub_mem_slitPlane_iff","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexRogersDilog.lean#L93-L98","doc":"`1 − z ∈ slitPlane ↔ z ∈ notCut` — both say `z ∉ [1,∞)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.hasDerivAt_cRogersL","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.hasDerivAt_cRogersL","kind":"theorem","line":58,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexRogersDilog.lean#L58-L84","doc":"**The derivative of the Rogers dilogarithm.**\n\n    L′(z) = −½·( log(1−z)/z + log z/(1−z) )\n\nThe `Li₂` term contributes `−log(1−z)/z` and the `½·log·log` term contributes\n`½·log(1−z)/z − ½·log z/(1−z)`; the two `log(1−z)/z` pieces combine to halve it.\nThis is exactly the `rogersDeriv` that\n`QOU.QBeta.FiveTwo.pentagon_deriv_x_eq_zero` takes as given. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.one_sub_ne_zero_of_mem_slitPlane","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.one_sub_ne_zero_of_mem_slitPlane","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexRogersDilog.lean#L53-L56","doc":"`1 − z ≠ 0` from `1 − z ∈ slitPlane`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.cRogersL","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.cRogersL","kind":"def","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ComplexRogersDilog.lean#L45-L51","doc":"The **Rogers dilogarithm** on `ℂ`, built on the integral continuation\n`cLiTwoExt` so that it is defined off `[1,∞)` rather than only on the disc.\n\nNeumann writes `R(z) = ½·log z·log(1−z) − ∫₀^z log(1−t)/t dt`; the integral is\n`−Li₂(z)`, so this is the same function. ","signatureChunk":0}]}